LIVE: HTTP 200
FRAGMENT True: you can effectively forward the entire SSH request from WSL to the ssh.exe process running on Windows
CONTEXT: 1password wsl integration leverages the interoperability built into wsl to forward ssh requests to the 1password ssh agent on windows instead of forwarding ssh agent requests like with standard openssh agent forwarding you can effectively forward the entire ssh request from wsl to the ssh exe process running on windows the ssh exe process then uses the 1password ssh agent on your windows host to authenticate the request this also means that any changes to your ssh configuration need to be made in your windows userprofile ssh config file rather than the file on your wsl instance forward an ssh request check if the 1password ssh agent is running on your windows host with the following command
